// The `trpc#6193` program shape, made non-buildable — RFC-0075 M1.
//
// The incident: a documented streaming idiom whose cleanup path silently never
// ran. `while (!opts.signal!.aborted)` kept looping with `aborted === false`
// after the client tab had closed, and a second reporter put it plainly — "our
// `return` method on the AsyncIterable is not being called after connection
// closes. This is causing a memory leak and our servers to OOM every couple of
// hours." The maintainer placed fault in the framework, not in user code. Eight
// months and five PRs later the fix was reverted, trading proxy correctness for
// a different leak.
//
// Every one of those programs typechecked. No amount of describing the SHAPE of
// a value says anything about whether its disposal runs. Ownership does, and the
// point of this RFC is that Vyrn already had the machinery — the same movecheck
// that governs owned values and divergent exits (RFC-0060).
//
// So the acquisition below is the error, not the missing cleanup: there is no
// line to point at for cleanup that was never written. That is what "an
// obligation, not a convention" means.
//
// This file is an INTENTIONAL compile error. It is meant to FAIL `vyrn check`,
// so the parity harness lists it under EXPECTED_CHECK_FAILURE rather than
// running it. Observe the diagnostics with:
//
//   vyrn check examples/stream_abandoned.vyrn
//
// Compare stream.vyrn, which discharges the obligation all three ways.

fn feed() -> Stream<Int64> {
    let xs: Array<Int64> = [1, 2, 3]
    return fromArray(xs)
}

fn main() -> Int64 {
    // Rejected: acquired here, never consumed and never closed.
    let events = feed()
    print(0)

    // Rejected: cleanup that exists but is not on every path — which is the
    // incident itself, in one line. The `else` path abandons it.
    let conditional = feed()
    if 1 == 1 {
        close(conditional)
    }

    // Rejected: leaving early skips the release below it.
    let early = feed()
    if 1 == 1 {
        return 1
    }
    close(early)

    return 0
}
